Yeah, I would tend to think that if your global model does not fit well then a model averaged version could not possibly be better.  Model averaging is meant to provide better out-of-sample prediction by avoiding overparameterization, while GOF testing simply suggests whether you have a model that could reasonably have generated the observed data.  So like Andy said, using the global model for GOF testing is probably adequate.

